# p5/payload/filemap -- THE payload declaration. scripts/build-p5-package.sh
# copies this file verbatim to <package>/payload/filemap, and p5-install reads
# it there (p5/bin/p5-install:265-285).
#
# FORMAT, exactly as p5-install parses it: mode|role|src|dest
#   mode  octal file mode, passed to `install -m`
#   role  client | server | both -- a row whose role is neither `both` nor the
#         installing box's role is SKIPPED, which is what makes one package
#         serve both boxes without either being a special case
#   src   path relative to the package's payload/ dir. It is the REPO path of
#         the file (ADR-005 section 4: source paths do not change), or a build/
#         path for something the builder produces rather than copies
#   dest  absolute production destination, from ADR-005 section 4's map
#
# NO PADDING SPACES. p5-install splits on `|` with a raw `read` and does not
# trim, so a column aligned with spaces becomes a mode/role/dest that carries
# them.
#
# EVERY DEST HERE IS A DECLARED ROW IN p5/contract/paths, and p5-install
# re-checks each one against contract/foreign, contract/namespace and
# contract/paths at install time (p5_check_dest, p5-common.sh:658). A dest that
# is not declared there is refused with exit 4 -- so this file cannot widen the
# namespace, only fill it.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE. THE LIST BELOW IS MECHANICAL, NOT PROSE, and
# that is the whole point of it (U176 folded into U211). Bar PK-4 in
# p5/test/run.sh takes every regular file under deploy/, subtracts the src
# column of the rows below, subtracts whatever scripts/build-p5-package.sh
# copies out of deploy/ as a PACKAGE TOOL (parsed from the builder, never
# hand-listed here, so the two cannot drift), and requires the remainder to be
# matched by the EXCLUDE globs below -- and the unaccounted set must be EMPTY.
# It also requires each file to be in EXACTLY ONE of the three, so a file that
# starts riding in the package as a tool must lose its EXCLUDE line in the same
# commit. So a new file under deploy/ is shipped, or it is deliberately not
# shipped WITH A REASON, and there is no third state where nobody noticed.
# Before PK-4 there was one: the three on-box validators sat in neither list,
# and the only way to get any of them onto a box was scp (U176).
#
# It is PK-4 and not PK-1 because p5/test/run.sh already had a PK-1 (every file
# a shipped program SOURCES is itself shipped -- the U124 xctl-lib defect). The
# two are the same idea one level apart: PK-1 asks whether the payload is enough
# for what it ships to RUN, PK-4 whether the payload is everything that should
# be in it.
#
# FORMAT of an entry: `# EXCLUDE|<glob>|<reason>`. The glob is matched with a
# POSIX `case`, where `*` spans `/`, so a `deploy/<dir>/*` entry covers every
# depth beneath it. Not a detail: U176's first cut of this check tested only a
# file's immediate parent and manufactured eight false findings out of the
# portal alone, and invented work is how a real finding gets lost. (U217 ships
# the portal, so that subtree glob is gone; the matcher rule is unchanged.)
#
# deploy/p5/shape-install and deploy/p5/shape/* have NO line here on purpose: since
# U210 the BUILDER copies them into the package (<pkg>/bin/p5-shape-install and
# <pkg>/shape/), which is account 2 above, and a file rides in exactly one account
# (PK-4 named all three DOUBLE-COUNTED at the U210+U211 merge, 2026-09-05).
# EXCLUDE|deploy/.gitkeep|placeholder that keeps the tree in git; not an artifact
# EXCLUDE|deploy/baseline/MANIFEST.sha256|the frozen P1-P3 baseline's own pin. It is rollback evidence ABOUT the old stack, not a P5 file
# EXCLUDE|deploy/p5/97-bond|the netifd hotplug hook. contract/paths leaves the two-digit priority UNSET on purpose (its `/etc/hotplug.d/iface/[0-9][0-9]-p5` glob row) -- choosing it is choosing an ordering against netifd's other hooks, which is E5's derivation to make and justify (p5/CONTRACT.md section 7, "What this contract does not settle", the hotplug-priority bullet -- cited by anchor, not line, per the U200 rule). The /etc/config/p5 row is withheld for the same class of reason: it is conditional on a decision E5 has not made
# EXCLUDE|deploy/p5/facts|the fact LEDGER: a design-time table checked on the PC by deploy/p5/test-facts.sh. Nothing on a box reads it
# EXCLUDE|deploy/p5/portal/README.md|the portal's own design/usage record, read in the repo. The other eight files under deploy/p5/portal/ are SHIPPED rows below (U217), so this is the only member of that subtree left with no destination; the whole-subtree glob it replaces went away in the same commit, because a file rides in exactly one account
# EXCLUDE|deploy/p5/test-facts.sh|PC-side checker for the fact ledger above; it runs in the repo, never on a box
# EXCLUDE|deploy/probe-capabilities.sh|operator-side measurement, run from the PC over ssh. It installs nothing and is not part of the product
# EXCLUDE|deploy/server/p5-server-measure.sh|operator-side measurement of the server, run from the PC
# EXCLUDE|deploy/server/mutant-check-p5-fw-deadman.sh|PC-side seeded A/B for the server firewall deadman
# EXCLUDE|deploy/server/test-p5-fw-deadman.sh|PC-side test of the server firewall deadman
# EXCLUDE|deploy/server/test-p5-server-footprint.sh|PC-side test of the server's memory footprint
# EXCLUDE|deploy/server/test-p5-server-init.sh|PC-side test of the server's procd service
#
# ARCHITECTURE. The two Go binaries are built GOOS=linux GOARCH=arm64: both
# boxes are aarch64 (.github/workflows/emulator-gate.yml:271-273 for the
# GL-MT2500 server, :738 for the client). p5/CONTRACT.md section 7 ("What this contract does not settle", the architecture bullet -- cited by anchor, not line, per the U200 rule) says the
# architecture choice is U28's and is expressed as filemap rows -- these two
# rows are that expression.
#
# mode|role|src|dest

