# ---- the on-box validators (G6/F23, U176 folded into U211) -----------------
# THE THREE TOOLS THAT SAY WHETHER AN INSTALL IS GOOD WERE NOT IN THE PACKAGE.
# Until these rows existed, deploy/p5/bond-accept -- which IS feature F23,
# "validates a P5 install on the box" -- the client preflight and the server
# preflight were in NEITHER the payload nor the exclusion list, so the only way
# to run any of them on a box was to scp it by hand: the exact hand-copy path
# the package exists to replace, and the one p5-install refuses for every other
# file because no contract row declared a destination (U176).
#
# THE PREMISE THAT HELD IT OPEN WAS FALSE, and it is worth naming because it is
# what made a three-row change look like a contract change: U176's row said
# "adding an install destination widens the namespace p5-install enforces".
# contract/namespace's `both|/usr/sbin/p5-*` row already admits all three names.
# These rows FILL that namespace; they do not widen it, and NS-2..NS-5 do not
# move.
#
# TWO PREFLIGHT NAMES, not one destination with two roles: the package
# builder's duplicate check keys on the DEST column alone ("two filemap rows
# claim the same destination"), so one dest carrying a client row and a server
# row would abort the build.
#
# ROLE SPLIT. p5-accept and p5-client-preflight are client-only: the acceptance
# runner drives the client's datapath, and the client preflight REFUSES without
# /etc/p5/transport.key, which makes it a post-install pre-switch check on the
# client. p5-server-preflight is server-only and read-only; it is ALSO run
# BEFORE the install, straight out of the unpacked package
# (`sh $PKG/payload/deploy/server/p5-server-preflight.sh`), which the package
# layout allows because payload/ carries every file at its repo path.
# Installing it as well is what lets an operator re-run it months later on a
# box whose /tmp no longer holds the package.
755|client|deploy/p5/bond-accept|/usr/sbin/p5-accept
755|client|deploy/p5/p5-client-preflight.sh|/usr/sbin/p5-client-preflight
755|server|deploy/server/p5-server-preflight.sh|/usr/sbin/p5-server-preflight

# ---- E4 shaping: the controller (U210) ------------------------------------
# Placed DISABLED like every other init script here; activation is the DAG's
# (act_shape_apply), and the leaves refuse to drive it unless it carries the
# P5 ownership marker on its line 3. The dest is P5's own name: the old
# spelling /etc/init.d/cake-autorate is P1's live service and a `p1|` row in
# contract/foreign, which p5_check_dest consults BEFORE the namespace, so a row
# at that dest is exit 4 (that is bar SH-10b's seed, and this unit's seed A).
755|client|deploy/p5/init.d/p5-shape|/etc/init.d/p5-shape

# ---- the portal (F17, U217) -----------------------------------------------
# Mo decided 2026-09-05 that the portal is built before deployment. That is the
# ONE decision docs/FEATURES.md F17 named -- a second uhttpd listener on the
# client -- and it covers all eight rows below. Nothing about the portal's
# behaviour changed to produce them: not a line of cgi/, lib/, www/, catalogue/
# or init.d/p5-portal moved.
#
# THE EXCLUDE GLOB `deploy/p5/portal/*` LEFT THE HEADER IN THIS SAME COMMIT.
# PK-4's rule is EXACTLY ONE account per file, so a subtree that starts shipping
# has to lose its exclusion in the commit that ships it or the bar names all
# eight DOUBLE-COUNTED. deploy/p5/portal/README.md is the one member of the
# subtree that still ships nowhere, so it kept a line of its own -- the glob was
# replaced by a file, not deleted.
#
# THE CGI'S DEST IS www/cgi-bin/p5-portal AND NOT cgi/p5-portal, and the reason
# is mechanical rather than stylistic: the init script starts uhttpd with
# `-h $DOCROOT -x /cgi-bin`, DOCROOT is /usr/lib/p5/portal/www
# (deploy/p5/portal/init.d/p5-portal:30,74), and uhttpd resolves the CGI prefix
# UNDER the docroot -- while the shipped page fetches the RELATIVE url
# `cgi-bin/p5-portal` (deploy/p5/portal/www/portal.js:15). So $DOCROOT/cgi-bin/
# p5-portal is the only destination at which the shipped page can reach the
# shipped CGI. deploy/p5/portal/README.md's Install section names both routes --
# "symlinked or installed at <docroot>/cgi-bin/p5-portal" -- and this is the one
# p5-install can express: it places FILES and records them by sha256, so a
# symlink would be a path nothing recorded and --remove would leave behind. The
# CGI resolves its library from $P5_PORTAL_DIR, never from its own directory
# (deploy/p5/portal/cgi/p5-portal:30), so the destination costs it nothing.
#
# PLACED DISABLED. p5-install enables nothing, here or anywhere: /etc/rc.d/
# S??p5-portal is written by `/etc/init.d/p5-portal enable`, which is an
# operator step. Two independent things keep an un-configured box quiet -- the
# absent rc.d flag, and the init script's own refusal to start with no
# /etc/p5/portal/port declared (init.d/p5-portal:57-59).
755|client|deploy/p5/portal/cgi/p5-portal|/usr/lib/p5/portal/www/cgi-bin/p5-portal
755|client|deploy/p5/portal/init.d/p5-portal|/etc/init.d/p5-portal
644|client|deploy/p5/portal/lib/portal-lib.sh|/usr/lib/p5/portal/lib/portal-lib.sh
644|client|deploy/p5/portal/catalogue/fields|/usr/lib/p5/portal/catalogue/fields
644|client|deploy/p5/portal/catalogue/logs|/usr/lib/p5/portal/catalogue/logs
644|client|deploy/p5/portal/catalogue/modes|/usr/lib/p5/portal/catalogue/modes
644|client|deploy/p5/portal/catalogue/probes|/usr/lib/p5/portal/catalogue/probes
644|client|deploy/p5/portal/www/index.html|/usr/lib/p5/portal/www/index.html
644|client|deploy/p5/portal/www/portal.js|/usr/lib/p5/portal/www/portal.js
